H(2, { module: 'Partner API', workflow: 'Events sent to partner systems (webhooks)', severity: 'P1', category: 'Reliability: lost events', where: 'src/backend/src/services/webhookService.js; table WebhookDelivery',
  evidence: 'Code read and test: a failed delivery was marked for retry and the retry lived only in the memory of the server instance, so it was lost on restart and never resumed (B-018). No staff action raised an event at all: a dispatch at the shipping desk told no partner. Nothing stopped the same event being recorded twice for a subscriber. A row was written after the business change, so a crash between the two lost the event.',
  expected: 'A business change and the events about it are saved together; each event reaches each subscriber once, is retried on a schedule, stops after a limit and can be sent again by a person.', actual: 'Events were best effort, raised only by partner calls, and lost on any failure.', cause: 'No durable queue and no link from the staff routes.',
  impact: 'A customer or carrier system that relies on events silently misses dispatches, deliveries and invoices.', dependencies: 'B-018, B-019.',
  correction: 'The existing WebhookDelivery table is used as an outbox. The row is written inside the transaction that makes the change (order confirmed, status changed, shipment dispatched, delivered, exception, invoice issued). Delivery claims a row with a conditional update, so several servers can run it at once; failures wait 1, 5, 30 and 120 minutes; after five tries the event is kept as failed; an administrator can send it again; a unique rule on (subscription, event) makes a second recording impossible (migration 20261113230000_webhook_delivery_once). No new infrastructure.',
  requiredTests: 'Delivered once; refused change leaves no event; backoff honoured; dead letter after five; replay; five runs at once; claim taken over after a crash.', status: 'VERIFIED FIXED',
  statusNote: 'The retry schedule runs only when the host calls the scheduled address (B-019, the owner\'s setting). Without it, an event is still sent right after the action, and a failed one waits until an administrator presses "Run now" on the Integrations screen.',
  verification: `${T4}, group "Event processing and background jobs": 13 scenarios, all pass. SQL Editor file 10 ran twice on the 85-branch copy with duplicate rows planted: the later duplicates were renamed, none deleted, and the second run changed nothing.` });
